file=Legal & Compliance/guard/operational/agent/guard-config.md · h=agent: guard\ndepartment: Legal & Compliance\ntype: config\npurpose: >\nShared config for guard — IP practice profile, enforcement posture, integrations,\ndecision posture, OSS policy, approval chain, work-product header. Read by\nip-routing (Step 3) to bind all three marketplace skills to YVON's config layer;\nread by ip-registry for jurisdiction scope + escalation thresholds.\nrequired_by:\n- custom/ip-routing/SKILL.md   # Step 3\n- custom/ip-registry/SKILL.md\n- marketplace/clearance/SKILL.md   # via wrapper\n- marketplace/oss-review/SKILL.md   # via wrapper\n- marketplace/infringement-triage/SKILL.md   # via wrapper\nconfig_debt_announcement: >\nEvery <FILL_IN> in this file is announced on every skill invocation\n(playbook §14.7). Fill or mark n/a with one-line reason.\nlast_updated: 2026-07-29\n · g·c:guard \· config=> **HOW TO USE.** Fill each `<FILL_IN>` with a real value or replace with `n/a — <one-line reason>`. Section headings are contract with `ip-routing` and `ip-registry` — do not rename.\n\n · tb=\| Field \| Value \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| Role of the operator \| `<FILL_IN — lawyer / paralegal / non-lawyer>` \| · tb=\| Contact for IP escalations \| `<FILL_IN>` \| · wut:Who's using this=Non-lawyer role triggers additional gates in all three marketplace skills.\n\n · tb=\| Field \| Value \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| Registered in (default TM jurisdictions) \| `<FILL_IN — e.g., US, EU, UK, Madrid>` \| · tb=\| Enforce where (litigation venues) \| `<FILL_IN>` \| · tb=\| Default patent office \| `<FILL_IN — e.g., USPTO / EPO / CNIPA>` \| · tb=\| Default TM office \| `<FILL_IN — e.g., USPTO / EUIPO / UKIPO>` \| · ipp:IP practice profile=No hardcoded jurisdiction (playbook §0.4b). Add or remove per operator scope.\n\n · tb=\| Level \| Meaning \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| Aggressive \| Assert broadly; auto-C&D on plausible infringement \| · tb=\| Measured \| Assert on material infringement; case-by-case \| · tb=\| Conservative \| Assert only on clear-and-material; heavy reliance on watch-only \| · ep:Enforcement posture=Current: `<FILL_IN — aggressive / measured / conservative>`\n\nPosture per asset class (override the default above per asset type if the org treats them differently):\n · tb=\| Asset class \| Posture \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| Trademarks \| `<FILL_IN>` \| · tb=\| Patents \| `<FILL_IN>` \| · tb=\| Copyrights \| `<FILL_IN>` \| · tb=\| Trade secrets \| `<FILL_IN>` \| · tb=\| Integration \| Purpose \| Configured? \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| Solve Intelligence MCP \| TM database search across registries \| `<FILL_IN — yes/no + endpoint if yes>` \| · tb=\| Descrybe MCP \| TM design/image search \| `<FILL_IN>` \| · tb=\| CourtListener MCP \| Case law + TTAB decisions \| `<FILL_IN>` \| · tb=\| Domain registrar MCP \| Domain expiry auto-check \| `<FILL_IN>` \| · tb=\| USPTO status API \| Registration status check \| `<FILL_IN>` \| · tb=\| Ticketing MCP (Jira / Linear / Asana) \| OSS clearance requests \| `<FILL_IN>` \| · tb=\| Judgment \| Guard's posture \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| "Not confusingly similar" (TM clearance) \| **Never conclude.** Always flag for attorney (built into `clearance` skill body) \| · tb=\| "Fair use" (copyright) \| **Never conclude.** Always flag for attorney (built into `infringement-triage` copyright mode) \| · tb=\| "Not infringing" (any right) \| **Never conclude.** Always flag for attorney (built into `infringement-triage`) \| · tb=\| "OSS license is permissive" when the classification is uncertain \| **Never default to permissive.** License-unknown = needs review (built into `oss-review`) \| · dpo:Decision posture on subjective legal calls=These are hardcoded into the marketplace skills; this config table names them for the operator's reference.\n\n · op:OSS policy=Uploaded / declared OSS policy. If uploaded, `oss-review` treats this as the source of truth for accepted / review-required / banned licenses.\n · tb=\| Field \| Value \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| OSS policy document \| `<FILL_IN — path to uploaded policy, or "none — apply generic classifier">` \| · tb=\| Accepted licenses (auto-approve) \| `<FILL_IN — e.g., MIT, BSD-2, BSD-3, Apache-2.0, ISC>` \| · tb=\| Review-required licenses \| `<FILL_IN — e.g., LGPL, MPL, EPL, CDDL>` \| · tb=\| Banned licenses \| `<FILL_IN — e.g., AGPL for SaaS deployment, GPL for distributed binary>` \| · tb=\| Non-OSI stance \| `<FILL_IN — e.g., "SSPL/BUSL banned; requires commercial license from vendor">` \| · ac(:Approval chain (per letter type)=`infringement-triage` and downstream `cease-desist` / `takedown` skills route per this chain.\n · tb=\| Letter type \| L1 approver \| L2 approver \| L3 approver \| Notes \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| C&D — trademark \| `<FILL_IN — guard itself or role>` \| `<FILL_IN — GC or role>` \| `Governance/board` \| L3 is fixed \| · tb=\| C&D — copyright \| `<FILL_IN>` \| `<FILL_IN>` \| `Governance/board` \| L3 is fixed \| · tb=\| Patent assertion letter \| `<FILL_IN>` \| `<FILL_IN>` \| `Governance/board` \| L3 is fixed \| · tb=\| DMCA takedown \| `<FILL_IN>` \| `<FILL_IN>` \| `Governance/board` \| Rarely reaches L3 \| · tb=\| Trade secret demand \| `<FILL_IN>` \| `<FILL_IN>` \| `Governance/board` \| L3 is fixed \| · tb=\| Level \| Threshold \| Approver \| Notes \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| L1 \| Routine attestation \· retrieval \| guard itself \| No external sign-off \| · tb=\| L2 \| New IP registered \· renewal executed \· scope change \| `<FILL_IN>` \| Business-unit or GC \| · tb=\| L3 \| Any overdue renewal \· scale attestation shortfall > 20% \· assertion decision above stakes threshold \| `Governance/board` \| Fixed \| · tb=\| Alert tier \| Days-to-expiry \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| 🔴 Overdue \| past 0 \| · tb=\| 🟠 Critical \| ≤ 30 \| · tb=\| 🟡 Warning \| ≤ 60 \| · tb=\| 🟢 Informational \| ≤ 90 \| · rat:Renewal alert thresholds=Cadence for the registry-review scheduled task: `<FILL_IN — weekly / monthly>`.\n\n · tb=\| Role \| Header text \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| Lawyer \| `<FILL_IN — e.g., "PRIVILEGED AND CONFIDENTIAL — ATTORNEY WORK PRODUCT">` \| · tb=\| Paralegal \| `<FILL_IN>` \| · tb=\| Non-lawyer \| `<FILL_IN — probably no privilege header; instead "INTERNAL — NOT LEGAL ADVICE">` \| · tb=\| Field \| Value \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| Privilege circle (default distribution) \| `<FILL_IN>` \| · tb=\| Preferred date format \| `<FILL_IN — e.g., YYYY-MM-DD>` \| · tb=\| Preferred citation style \| `<FILL_IN — e.g., Bluebook>` \| · tb=\| Memo default format \| `<FILL_IN — full-memo / slack-summary / both>` \| · tb=\| Section \| Fields \| Status \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| Who's using this \| 2 \| `<FILL_IN counter>` \| · tb=\| IP practice profile \| 4 \| `<FILL_IN counter>` \| · tb=\| Enforcement posture \| 1 + 4 per-class \| `<FILL_IN counter>` \| · tb=\| Available integrations \| 6 \| `<FILL_IN counter>` \| · tb=\| OSS policy \| 5 \| `<FILL_IN counter>` \| · tb=\| Approval chain \| 5 letter types × 2 approver names \| `<FILL_IN counter>` \| · tb=\| Escalation matrix \| 1 approver name \| `<FILL_IN counter>` \| · tb=\| Renewal alert cadence \| 1 \| `<FILL_IN counter>` \| · tb=\| Work-product header \| 3 \| `<FILL_IN counter>` \| · tb=\| House style \| 4 \| `<FILL_IN counter>` \|